// The `const ref` argument position. See tests/xfail/lit_oob_local for the rule.
//
// Its own fixture rather than a line in lit_oob_argument, because the two positions do not share an
// emitter path: a by-value literal is passed straight through, while a `ref` one is materialised into a
// temp (emitReorderedCall's `__primtmp` arm). That arm takes the PARAMETER's C type, which is only sound
// because the literal was range-checked against that same type first — this fixture is what says so.
fn void take(const ref int8 x) { }
fn int32 main() {
    take(x: 300);
    return 0;
}
